 "response": "Getosti's budget is now **$2095K**.\n\n**Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget entries change the budget. Everything else is ignored. That covers notes, emails, chats, tickets and calls from other teams, and Finance Office items that do not touch the budget (rooms, cost centre codes, audits).\n\n**Withdrawals.** Some withdrawals are themselves withdrawn, so each chain is resolved from its last link back to the original update:\n- An update stays in force when its withdrawal is cancelled. For example, #0002 survives because #0161 cancels #0081, which re-activates #0032. #0032 cancels #0015, which re-activates #0009, and #0009 cancels #0007, the withdrawal of #0002.\n- An update is removed when the chain ends in a working withdrawal. For example, #0003 is removed because #1164 cancels #0154, which re-activates #0021. #0021 cancels #0013, leaving #0012's withdrawal of #0003 in effect.\n\nIn total, 106 budget updates end up withdrawn. They include #0003, #0006, #0020, #0022, #0029, #0033, #0036, #0099, #0384, #0533, #0568, #1131 and #1430.\n\n**Calculation.** Starting from the $1730K set in #0001, I applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in record order. The last change is the $25K decrease in #1590, which brings the total to $2095K. This is a single running total; I did not do a separate second pass to check it.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
